  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f6b37b60-80e6-4d11-9ee0-747f148b0a11-Untitled-tower.png\" style=\"width: 369px; height: 308px;\" />Let&nbsp;the height of the tower <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></math> be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math></p><p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>{</mo><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>M</mi></math> is the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>}</mo></math></p><p>Now in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> In a triangle sides opposite to equal angles are</p><p>equal<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math> )</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math></p><p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi></math></p><p>By using Equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mo>(</mo><mn>200</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo></math> {By using Pythagoras theorem}</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> From <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mo>(</mo><mn>200</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>h</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mo>(</mo><mn>40000</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>40000</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math> {By squaring both the sides}</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>40000</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>10000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>",
